title A declaration is not an exemption -- the report card learns two blessed constructions
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, condense ITINERARY and refill Now, send each finished increment
think Lap index from git log --oneline | wc -l = 3419, unchanged from the prior lap, because that lap staged its work and never committed it. So the council rota reads row 3419 mod 5 = 4 again -- Earth and Mercury, the concrete: the one-clock naming law, Two Rooms, the marked value. Two Rooms governed directly. The card publishes four numbers into the checkable room, and this lap found two of them measuring something other than what they claim.
think First duty was the prior lap's own close. Fourteen files sat staged with a written session log and two closed REDS rows, and ITINERARY's own standing line says a lap ends at the commit rather than at git add (REDS %188). Committed it as its own signed round and pushed both remotes before opening anything new, so the increment is followable rather than folded into mine.
think The commit-msg hook refused the first body -- 244 words, 1 mechanism word, wanted 3. It was right: I had written module_count() and modules and let the tooling word count stand for engineering vocabulary. Named the shell function, the scan file, and the new script plainly and it welcomed the second.
think Opened the lap with the roster COLD before touching anything: 57 guards, 57 green, guards_red=0. Standfast satisfied, and no open agent-closable row stands in construction/REDS.md -- every row carries CLOSED.
think Took the round the prior lap's recommend line named. Reach has no honest denominator on a page that is mostly links, and Truth misreads a placeholder shape. Both are one finding wearing two faces: a meter that instructs a repair which would make the artifact worse is the thing to fix.
think Measured the population before writing a line, which is REDS %213's lesson applied. Four living pages declare an index in their header. Three carry 13, 13, and 10 words of prose. The fourth, docs-geode/edu/README.md, carries 193 and already read A at 3 cross-references per hundred words. So the two-condition rule discriminated on real data before it existed in code, and the fourth row is the whole argument for the floor.
think Chose 100 words for the floor because that is the fault stated as a number rather than a threshold picked for feel: a rate expressed per hundred words is extrapolation below one full unit of its own denominator.
think Guarded the declaration with a second condition on purpose. A self-declared exemption is a door, and a door beside a wall makes the wall a habit again. Declaration alone would let any page type Kind index into its header and leave the meter; word count alone would exempt every short page. Neither half opens it.
think Read the declaration in the HEADER only -- the block above the first --- rule -- so a body that merely discusses indexes declares nothing, and planted that as its own control reading.
think For Truth, narrowed to the two placeholder runs the naming law actually spells inside a path shape, YYYYMMDD and HHMMSS. Asked git rather than guessing: zero tracked paths in this tree carry either literally, and exactly 8 such links stand across all living Markdown in 4 files. NNN was tempting and left out -- it is a ledger sigil rather than part of a path shape, so including it would have been speculative.
think Kept the other half deliberately: a fabricated stamp naming no file still costs twenty points. That is the exact failure the same law warns about, and it is what keeps the placeholder reading a reading rather than an escape hatch.
obs Then proved the control bites, which is the half a passing run cannot show. Pointed at a copy of the card carrying the old rule, it refused 11 of 17 and passed 6 -- and one of those passes was false. The declared-short probe had put its links in a BULLET list, and the reach reading skips list lines, so the links were never counted and the probe passed against the old rule too.
obs That was worth catching. A reading that passes for the wrong reason is worth less than no reading, because it looks like coverage. Rewrote the plant to carry its links in a prose line, mirroring docs/README.md's own header line, and tightened the body-declaration reading to require the field rather than accept its absence. The control now refuses 13 of 17 and passes exactly 4 -- and those 4 are the readings describing behavior that must NOT change: a long declaring page still penalized, a short undeclaring page still penalized, a fabricated stamp still counted and still named.
obs The door roster's below-B ceiling fell from 1 to 0 by measurement rather than by edit. docs/README.md reads A+ on its counted half with no word of it rewritten, and all 12 door documents now read B or better. That is the point of fixing a meter instead of the page it misread.
obs Graded every artifact touched. The essay reads A 94 at Field. context/GAUGE_STYLE.md reads A. Three of the four touched scripts read A or A+ at Meter.
obs The fourth pushed one frame: qa_report_card_control.sh reads F, 30 of 30 cited paths unresolved. Those paths are planted heredoc fixtures -- a document meter pointed at a script. Measured before deciding, since measurement at molt time is allowed to close a frame: the related real asymmetry is that Reach skips fenced code blocks and Truth does not, worth 5 links across 4 files, none on any roster. Closed the frame with the number and left both findings as ITINERARY lines rather than patching a third reading at the end of a long lap.
obs Being honest about that call: this is the third instance of one class -- the card reading a construction it does not understand. A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom, so the class is named on the card by name rather than left for a fourth lap to rediscover.
loom roster cold_guards=57 cold_green=57 cold_red=0
loom qa_card door_documents=12 below_b_before=1 below_b_after=0 ceiling=0
loom qa_index declaring_pages=4 under_floor=3 over_floor=1 floor_words=100
loom qa_truth placeholder_runs=2 tracked_paths_carrying_them=0 living_links_matched=8 files=4
loom control behaviors=44 new=17 old_rule_refused=13 old_rule_passed=4
file tools/fixtures/qa_report_card.sh Reach reads a page's own header declaration under two conditions; Truth reads a placeholder shape as an illustration
file tools/fixtures/qa_report_card_control.sh 17 new readings, each planted from both sides, the index probe carrying its links in prose rather than bullets
file tools/fixtures/qa_report_card_scan.sh the below-B ceiling falls 1 -> 0, with the reason written beside the number
file tools/q/qa_report_card_witness.rish 17 asserts added, 44 behaviors, header rewritten to name both readings and the bite count
file context/GAUGE_STYLE.md the four-readings table names both shapes, and a new section argues them
file active-designing/20260825-034444_a-declaration-is-not-an-exemption.md the two-condition form, and the three questions it reaches past this card
file construction/ITINERARY.md Now refilled with the round and the two measured next doors; one lap row shelved to hold the bound
file construction/archive/20260825-003210_itinerary-landed-laps.md the shelved row, link depth moved with it
recommend keep-going the register denominator is the next round -- docs-geode/libraries/README.md reads Register 0 off ONE surviving sentence, which is the same extrapolation fault one reading over; measure the sentence-count distribution across the 130 living pages first, decide whether a floor or a report is the honest answer, and plant it in qa_report_card_control.sh from both sides before touching the number
